## Workflows

### Working on <core domain>

Authoritative sources; cross-check before answering or changing:

- `<path/to/source-of-truth>`: <why it's authoritative; which way the dependency points>

Approach:

1. Read the relevant authoritative source first; quote/cite it when explaining behavior.
2. For non-trivial changes, propose the diff and confirm before writing — `<HIGH_IMPACT_PATHS>`
   are shared across the repo; always confirm.
3. After a non-trivial change, fan out **in parallel** (one message, multiple subagent calls)
   to the relevant **read-only reviewers** and reconcile before declaring done. Verdicts are
   advisory: fix real issues, push back if wrong. Pin the read-only subagent type so they
   can't write.
   - `<area>-reviewer`: change touches `<area path>`

### Recording changes (changesets)

Changesets are the canonical changelog: one `.changeset/*.md` per meaningful change,
consumed by `changeset version` at release time. After completing a user-visible change and
**before the user commits**, run the `/changeset` skill (or spawn `changeset-writer`). It
inspects the diff, picks patch/minor/major per package, and records via
`node .claude/scripts/changeset-write.mjs` (validates package names against the workspace).
Nothing release-worthy? Record that too: `changeset-write.mjs --empty --summary "<why>"`.
Never hand-edit `CHANGELOG.md` or `.changeset/*.md`.

### Planning non-trivial features

Enter plan mode (or spawn a `Plan` subagent) and clarify scope first. Include: problem,
proposed solution, architecture notes, phased breakdown, todo checklist, open questions.

### Tracking out-of-scope work

Discover a real issue outside current scope? **Do not fix it inline**; log it and keep moving —
run the `/backlog-add` skill (backed by `node .claude/scripts/backlog-log.mjs`).

- Prefixes by area: `<PREFIX>` (`<path>`), ...
- After every add, the skill spawns `backlog-reviewer` to validate/dedupe/gut-check; reconcile first.
- On resolving an item while shipping: `node .claude/scripts/backlog-log.mjs remove <ID> <file> "<resolution>"`.
- No wishlist/vague items, and nothing already covered by an active plan.

### Debugging with end-to-end tracing

For bugs needing more than a one-shot fix: form hypotheses first, then add structured
instrumentation under `.claude/debug/`. Track every code-path edit so it can be removed.
Delete the instrumentation once fixed — the dir should only hold active investigations.

